<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Friday, barrows and gilts were $0.50 higher. Top $46.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Interior Iowa moved 97,000 hogs Friday and 19,000 Saturday. Springtime in the air and farmers back in town.</p>
<p>Packer demand was good as Easter's on it's way.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    46.00-46.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    44.50-45.50</p>
<p>    US 2-4	290-310 lbs    42.50-43.50</p>
<p>    US 1-2 package  228 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady/off $1.00. Top $50.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2	300-450 lbs    44.00</p>
<p>		    450-500 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3	500-550 lbs    47.00</p>
<p>		    550-700 lbs    49.00-50.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	300-700 lbs    40.50</p>
<p>		    200-300 lbs    41.50</p>
</text>
